# .claude/settings.json: live CC user state (theme etc). install.sh jq-merges the
# tracked hooks fragment into ~/.claude/settings.json rather than stow-linking it.
.claude/settings.hooks.json
# .mcp.json: project-scope MCP entry, only meaningful with cwd=~/dotfiles. NOT
# stowed to ~/.mcp.json - that would make every claude session with cwd=$HOME
# pick up a pending-approval project server (+ a ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} warning).
# The reliable path is the user-scope registration install.sh do_claude() adds.
.mcp.json
# .config/cliamp/config.toml: the TRACKED copy uses password =
# "${NAVIDROME_PASSWORD}", but cliamp does NOT interpolate env vars in every
# build, so the live file holds the real credential. Deliberately NOT stowed and
# deliberately NOT in stow-drift's compareOnly (that demands byte-identical,
# which is exactly wrong here - the two copies MUST differ). Never copy the live
# file back over the tracked one: the password has never been committed (verified
# 2026-08-30, 0 hits across all history) and must stay that way. Live settings
# that are safe to share (theme/provider/visualizer) get hand-synced.
.config/cliamp/config.toml
